{"user": "what is the best technique", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:14.116876+00:00", "assistant": "At this point the board is full, so there\u2019s no move left \u2014 final is **White 43, Black 21**.\n\nBest endgame technique: **count the finish, don\u2019t chase big flips.**\n\nUse this order:\n\n1. **Corners first** \u2014 once you own a corner, it can\u2019t be flipped.\n2. **Avoid giving corners** \u2014 don\u2019t play next to an empty corner unless it\u2019s safe.\n3. **Mobility** \u2014 make moves that leave White with few or no legal moves.\n4. **Stable edges** \u2014 edge discs connected to corners are hard to change.\n5. **Count final discs** \u2014 ask: \u201cAfter both players finish, who has more?\u201d not \u201cHow many do I flip now?\u201d\n\nIn your final board, White\u2019s corners/edges became stable, so Black couldn\u2019t catch up even with middle flips.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:21.777943+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:24.897382+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Pri