{"user": "I meant generally in the game what is the best technique", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:41.939280+00:00", "assistant": "Generally, the best Othello technique is:\n\n1. **Corners are king**  \n   A corner disc can never be flipped. If you can safely take a corner, it\u2019s usually huge.\n\n2. **Don\u2019t play next to empty corners**  \n   Squares like **b1, a2, b2** near corner **a1** often give your opponent the corner.\n\n3. **Mobility > big flips**  \n   A \u201cgood\u201d move often flips only a few discs but leaves White with very few legal moves.\n\n4. **Edges are good only when stable**  \n   Edges connected to your corner are strong. Random edge discs can still be flipped or used against you.\n\n5. **Endgame: count, don\u2019t guess**  \n   In the last few moves, try to count the final disc total after both players move.\n\nSimple rule of thumb:  \n**Don\u2019t ask \u201cHow many discs do I flip now?\u201d Ask \u201cWhat good moves will White have after this?\u201d**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:43.966721+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:48.219993+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 2, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 0.6666666666666666, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Solution Request"], "llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction", "Hint"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "