{"user": "why can corners not be flipped", "user_ts": "2026-08-07T15:39:55.057277+00:00", "assistant": "Corners can\u2019t be flipped because a disc only flips when it is **trapped between two opponent discs in a straight line**.\n\nA corner is at the **end of the board**, so there is no square \u201cbehind\u201d it. That means it can never be sandwiched.\n\nExample: for **a1** to be flipped, White would need to trap it from the other side \u2014 but the \u201cother side\u201d is off the board. Impossible.\n\nSo once you take a corner, it is **permanent** for the rest of the game.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-07T15:40:02.076196+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-07T15:40:04.313958+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant": {"final": ["Direct Instruction"], "consensus": ["Direct Instruction"], "votes": {"Direct Instruction": 3}, "confidence": {"Direct Instruction": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Direct Instruction"], "llama": ["Direct Instruction"], "sonnet": ["Direct Instruction"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"Worked Line": 1, "General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"Worked Line": 0.3333333333333333, "General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Worked Line", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, 